WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.920
It gives me no pleasure to&nbsp;
bring this to you today.&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:09.200
It's a milestone that we've been&nbsp;
warning about for months at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:16.400
and it's a horrible milestone as coronavirus&nbsp;
cases and subsequently deaths have climbed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:22.880
We hit 2000 deaths per day again and we went past&nbsp;
that. I've been saying that by the end of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:30.720
month, we will likely be seeing a 9/11 day worth&nbsp;
of deaths every single day from coronavirus. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:38.080
we are essentially there. Yesterday was the worst&nbsp;
single death day since the start of the pandemic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:43.520
Twenty eight hundred thirty three people died in&nbsp;
one day. Depending on how you measure the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.800
the exact 24 hours, Johns Hopkins actually has a&nbsp;
higher number above three thousand. But this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:56.720
roughly, essentially the number of people killed&nbsp;
on 9/11 directly by the events. Now, the number,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.840
it's twenty nine, seventy seven, I believe, is&nbsp;
the official number of 9/11 deaths on 9/11. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:07.760
this doesn't include people that died in the&nbsp;
days after due to stress induced heart attacks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.960
and and first responders who later developed&nbsp;
illness because of their presence at Ground Zero.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:18.480
So the number is really quite a bit higher. But&nbsp;
on the day of 9/11, at the sites of the disaster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.960
it's considered to be just under three&nbsp;
thousand. And that's where we are. We are likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:29.040
to significantly exceed this daily death&nbsp;
number for much of the remaining month.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:36.800
And half the country is barely willing to&nbsp;
alter their lives in any way as a result.&nbsp;

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:46.160
And 9/11 is an interesting event to think about&nbsp;
because think back to 9/11. We as a result of one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:54.400
day of 3000 people tragically dying, completely&nbsp;
reformed airport security, and created a massive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.400 --> 00:02:01.840
I mean gargantuan infrastructure through which&nbsp;
we now all go when we fly. TSA was created,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:08.720
the Patriot Act was passed justifying invasions&nbsp;
of privacy on the basis of keeping us safe.&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:14.400
We attacked a country and got involved in a multi&nbsp;
decade military engagement. The wrong country,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:20.720
by the way, we, I believe, also created&nbsp;
the Department of Homeland Security,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:28.560
may be another agency, all because of 9/11. And&nbsp;
now we have a 9/11 every day at this point, 300000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.920
approaching 300000 dead nationally from&nbsp;
the entire pandemic. And nearly half the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:41.200
country doesn't want to do anything about this&nbsp;
nine elevens worth of deaths every single day.&nbsp;

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:49.280
Now, as a reminder, covid deaths, lag cases. At&nbsp;
this point, it's by about a month. We are now at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:56.640
about 100000 people hospitalized nationally with&nbsp;
the virus. That's a record, which means that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:02.800
next month is going to be absolutely insane. And&nbsp;
as you can see, when you look at a chart of cases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:08.320
of those hospitalized and deaths, you see&nbsp;
hospitalizations are approaching nearly double&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:13.120
the record we had. We had about sixty thousand&nbsp;
hospitalizations during the first spike in April.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:19.760
We had about sixty thousand hospitalized in the&nbsp;
second spike in July. We are now at about one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:26.160
hundred thousand hospitalized and continuing to&nbsp;
climb. Notice how deaths track hospitalizations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:32.400
In the second spike, deaths didn't climb as much,&nbsp;
and that's because hospitals had more capacity. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:38.320
are now starting to see hospitals fill up again&nbsp;
and it all bodes really, really poorly. Now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:45.120
we're expecting vaccine approval for one vaccine&nbsp;
next week, another vaccine shortly thereafter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.720
It will take months to roll that out. The numbers&nbsp;
we might see in the rest of December into January,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:55.920
into February, even into March, depending on how&nbsp;
quickly these vaccines are deployed, these are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:01.280
going to be completely nightmarish numbers.&nbsp;
We're almost living in two realities. Sadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:06.720
you look at what public health experts say and we&nbsp;
have a dire, disastrous situation. You look at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:12.480
Instagram and Facebook pages of nearly half the&nbsp;
country, people behaving like nothing is going on.&nbsp;

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:17.520
It is truly nuts. And the next month&nbsp;
is next month is going to be terrible.

